# Code Documentation: How to use for beginners

## Finances Automation
**This file is designed to create a new invoice whenever a school registers.**

Upon registration, it pulls from:

Gmail - the schools that registered but have not been processed by this code

Airtable - the registration data for that school

This code then generates a new invoice sheets file from the correct template, fills in the right columns for Finances in Airtable,
and fills in the new invoice sheets file. It also generates an email in Google Docs based on a template with placeholders, sharing it with SG@SCVMUN.COM
### How to use it:
When you get an email from Airtable, run this code on your local machine. You can run it in VScode, or a termainal. Do specify if it is an independent delegate (use your own discretion)

You're here for a reason! Check whatever this code generates; it will give you links to the files.

Contact the SG once you're done.

If something breaks (python returns an error), ask the USG of Logistics.

## Copying Invoices
**This file is designed to copy over an invoice when you move from one range to another**

When run, it takes from the user inputs on what it is copying to (i.e. from Invoice 1 to 2). 

Scans the attending folder for all school folders. Looks inside for folders from this year's folder.

Then for each school, it finds the sheet you're copying from, and makes a new sheet based on that.

Moves the cells in the new sheet based on pre-set rules with fees.

Prints out a list of sheets needing edits, and sheets that it did not touch.

### How to use it:
Most of the time, the text gives you hints on what to do. Just follow instructions, click the links needed (edit things manually if necessary).

Please take the time to select a few schools for result review.

## Invoice Final Data
**This one prints out a new CSV File with all invoice data**

When you run it, the code scans the folder set in the script.

For each sheet inside that folder, it extracts the balance, comments, and school name.

Makes a new CSV with columns as Name, Balance, and Comments.

### How to use it:
Ensure that the folderID is correct inside the variable.

Run it, and go to the file path it gives you for the new CSV. You can import it into Google Sheets for better viewing.

This is mainly designed for right before SCVMUN, when you need to see which schools still owe you money.

